@tradition window-sketch
// SW2, 0.92.6 item 7(a), week 7 (FX17's shape: Saturday 11:45, a quiet room: the observatory, not the bridge deck).
// Window sketching: every 8 weeks from Day 48. Paper and pencils at the observatory windows; everyone draws what's
// outside (Tavessa ahead, the dust, the hull). Luca Alvarez hosts (Survey; off Saturdays; takes his Gerald to the
// observatory). Theo Teague, who drew comics, left on Day 21 (CS1). Quiet: anim read.
k: 714
title: Window sketching
when: every 8 weeks saturday week 7 from day 43
at: 11:45-12:30
min: 20
where: 2 room Observatory: common-room
where: 2 room Science corridor: bench
hold: 1
who: alvarez-luca always, stargazer 50%, window-seat 40%, quiet-corner 30%, everyone 8%
anim: read
host: alvarez-luca
from: alvarez-luca
invite: host=alvarez-luca odds=25% line="Window sketching at the observatory! Bring nothing. I've got pencils. And Gerald."

== mail
- Window sketching tomorrow, {time}, at the observatory. Paper and pencils provided. Draw what's out there. Nobody has to be good at it.

== ask
- Window sketching at the observatory this morning. Alvarez brings the pencils.
- Sketching later. I can't draw. That's allowed, apparently.   #funny

== here
- Shh. I'm doing the stars. All of them.   #funny
- That's Tavessa. The smudge. My smudge is better.   #funny
- Can I borrow the grey pencil?

== thanks
- You take a pencil and a sheet of paper to the observatory window. Everyone draws what's out there, quietly.   #warm

== chatter
- I drew Tavessa at window sketching. It looks like a sneeze.   #funny
- Alvarez put everyone's sketch up on the wall after. Mine too.   #warm
- Window sketching. The quietest hour I've had all week.
